---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Privacy requests, including deletion for people who cannot sign in.
const contact = 'contact@bikes.pizza';
const updated = 'September 24, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Delete your account · bikes.pizza"
  description="How to delete your bikes.pizza account, what is removed, and what stays."
>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-light tracking-wide text-ink">Delete your account</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted text-sm font-light">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-ink font-light leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <p>
          You can delete your bikes.pizza account yourself at any time, from the
          app or from this website. Deletion is immediate and cannot be undone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">In the app</h2>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-decimal list-outside pl-6">
          <li>Open the <span class="text-ink">Settings</span> tab and sign in if you are not already.</li>
          <li>Scroll to the bottom and tap <span class="text-ink">Delete account</span>.</li>
          <li>Confirm with <span class="text-ink">Delete</span>.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">On the website</h2>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-decimal list-outside pl-6">
          <li>
            Go to the{' '}
            <a href="/account" class="text-spice hover:underline">account page</a>{' '}
            and sign in.
          </li>
          <li>Scroll to <span class="text-ink">Delete account</span> and click <span class="text-ink">Delete my account</span>.</li>
          <li>Confirm.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">If you cannot sign in</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Write to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="text-spice hover:underline">{contact}</a>{' '}
          from the email address on the account and ask for it to be deleted. We
          will confirm with you and delete it, normally within a few days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">What is deleted</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
          <li>Your sign-in details and your email address as an account identifier.</li>
          <li>Your username and profile page. The username becomes available for someone else to choose.</li>
          <li>Your passkeys and any authenticator enrollment.</li>
          <li>Your comments (except placeholders where others have replied), your reactions, and every conversation you were in, both sides included.</li>
          <li>Your newsletter choices.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">What stays</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Posts that have already been published stay on bikes.pizza, credited to
          the username they were published under, together with the record of
          the submission behind them. Posts are part of a public archive and are
          not tied to an account; the{' '}
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-spice hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>{' '}
          explains why, and how to ask for a post to be removed. No other data is
          kept.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
